What was ported from T3 Code (reimplemented in Python and vanilla JavaScript; no T3 code is
bundled or required at runtime):

- Page layout and behavior: apps/web/src/components/usage/ (UsagePage, UsageProviderChart,
  UsageShareBar, UsageModelDialog, UsageLimits, UsagePriceOverrides, usageBreakdown,
  usageProviders, usageShortcuts, usagePagePreferences).
- Shared logic: packages/shared/src/usageFormat.ts, usageMerge.ts and usageLimits.ts.
- Scanning, de-duplication, aggregation and pricing: apps/server/src/usage/ (UsageService,
  usageAggregation, usagePricing, usageTranscriptReader).
- Provider readers: the Claude, Codex, OpenCode, Grok, Antigravity and Pi usage readers, and
  the Claude and Codex limits mapping.
- Provider labels and colors.

Model prices come from LiteLLM (https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm, MIT), fetched at run time.
